  "passage": {
    "text": "Every farm has costs. Farmers buy seeds, fertilizer, fuel and feed for their livestock. They pay for machinery and repairs. They also pay wages and taxes. Some costs are fixed, for example the rent for the land. Other costs change every month. A new tractor is much more expensive than an old one, so Tomas bought a used machine last year. In spring, farmers spend a lot on seeds. In autumn, they get income from the harvest. Tomas keeps a record of all his expenses. He wants to know where his money goes.",
